# CODEOWNERS: who GitHub asks to review a pull request that touches a path.
#
# It routes reviews and enforces nothing here. The `main` ruleset (scripts/github-settings.sh) requires 0 approvals
# and does not turn on "require review from code owners": GitHub never lets you approve your own pull request, so
# with a single owner that rule would block every merge (or force an admin bypass, which the ruleset doesn't have).
# A team with a second reviewer can raise the approvals and turn the rule on (wiki/github-repository-settings.md).
#
# `@your-org` is a placeholder: infra/adapt/adopt.sh stamps the owner of REPOSITORY (adopt.conf) over it. Use a
# user or a team (@org/team); GitHub ignores an owner without write access.

*                    @your-org
/.github/            @your-org
/scripts/            @your-org
/infra/security/     @your-org
/charts/             @your-org
